End-to-end process flow
1. Project scaffolding

main.py creates a new project from the trend_following pipeline template. It generates starter project files such as config, whitelist, and run script, with the goal of creating repeatable optimisation projects rather than manually assembling each run.

SE skills shown: project scaffolding, automation, template-driven project creation.

2. Configuration loading and validation

The generated run.py loads config.yaml, validates it, then executes the predefined stages in sequence.

SE skills shown: configuration-driven design, validation, reproducible setup.

3. Staged pipeline execution

The trend-following process runs:

Trigger
  ↓
Conformation / Confirmation
  ↓
Trendline
  ↓
Volume
  ↓
Exit

Each stage is executed independently through StageRunner, then a result YAML file is created for the selected indicator before the next stage continues.

SE skills shown: workflow orchestration, modular pipeline design, stage isolation.

4. StageRunner orchestration

StageRunner creates the stage output folders, clears MT5 test cache, optionally regenerates Expert Advisors, then runs the optimisation workflow for that stage.

SE skills shown: process orchestration, filesystem management, automation of repeatable workflows.

5. Expert Advisor generation

For each candidate indicator in a stage, the framework generates EA source files from templates and YAML indicator definitions, then compiles them for MT5 execution.

SE skills shown: code generation, templating, YAML-driven behaviour, external compiler integration.

6. MT5 initialisation and execution

The framework generates MT5 strategy tester .ini files, runs MT5 through CLI automation, and executes optimisation/backtest jobs for each generated EA.

SE skills shown: external process automation, CLI integration, batch execution, Windows tooling automation.

7. IS/OOS evaluation

Each candidate is tested using in-sample and out-of-sample evaluation. The aim is to avoid selecting candidates that only perform well on the optimisation window. The project README also describes IS/OOS evaluation as part of the workflow.

SE skills shown: simulation workflow design, validation logic, optimisation evaluation.

8. Result parsing and scoring

After MT5 runs complete, the framework parses result files, extracts optimisation outputs, creates summaries, and identifies top-performing parameter sets.

SE skills shown: data processing, result aggregation, metric-based evaluation, pandas-style workflow processing.

9. Manual candidate selection

After each stage, the user manually reviews results and selects which indicator should progress. The run template explicitly creates placeholder result YAML files and expects the user to replace indicator_tbd with the selected indicator.

SE skills shown: human-in-the-loop workflow design, stage-gated processing, controlled progression.

10. Downstream stage construction

Later stages incorporate the selected outputs from earlier stages. For example, the Confirmation stage is built around the selected Trigger, Trendline builds on earlier choices, and so on.

SE skills shown: staged dependency management, progressive system construction, modular composition.

